WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.040 --> 00:00:05.980
With a mysterious new villain, a surprise
twist and big changes for all of our favourite

00:00:05.980 --> 00:00:10.120
characters, the Witcher Season 2 has tons
of details we need to discuss.

00:00:10.120 --> 00:00:14.080
Yippee-ki-yay, movie lovers, I'm Jan and in
this video I'm explaining everything you might

00:00:14.080 --> 00:00:18.110
have missed in the ending of Season 2 and
what it all means for Season 3.

00:00:18.110 --> 00:00:20.630
Spoilers ahead, of course, so take care.

00:00:20.630 --> 00:00:26.300
Key to understanding the Season 2 finale is
the Deathless Mother, aka Voleth Meir, a demon

00:00:26.300 --> 00:00:28.160
who takes possession of Ciri.

00:00:28.160 --> 00:00:33.000
According to Vesemir, the first witchers imprisoned
Voleth Meir in a hut long ago.

00:00:33.000 --> 00:00:34.610
One of the oldest monsters.

00:00:34.610 --> 00:00:35.610
A demon.

00:00:35.610 --> 00:00:38.630
She wreaked havoc until the witchers bound
her deep in the forest.

00:00:38.630 --> 00:00:44.490
However, the demon woke from her slumber after
Ciri's scream split the monolith outside Cintra.

00:00:44.490 --> 00:00:49.190
She begins by appearing in the dreams of Yennefer,
Fringilla, and Queen of the Elves Francesca,

00:00:49.190 --> 00:00:51.640
and manipulates their fears and personal pain.

00:00:51.640 --> 00:00:57.150
For Yennefer, the demon taunts her about her
loss of power after Sodden Hill and promises

00:00:57.150 --> 00:01:00.620
it back if she takes Ciri to the broken monolith
by Cintra.

00:01:00.620 --> 00:01:05.260
For Fringilla, the Deathless Mother spurs
her on to take power for herself by forming

00:01:05.260 --> 00:01:07.030
an alliance with the Elves.

00:01:07.030 --> 00:01:11.310
This leads the Nilfgaardians to mistrust the
sorceress and when she uncovers their plot

00:01:11.310 --> 00:01:15.900
and takes revenge, you can hear Voleth Meir
cackling in the background feeding off the

00:01:15.900 --> 00:01:18.230
pain and destruction she's sown.

00:01:18.230 --> 00:01:23.380
As for Francesca, the demon takes the form
of the legendary Elven prophet Ithlinne who

00:01:23.380 --> 00:01:27.729
preys on her insecurity about never having
brought a baby to term and promises she'll

00:01:27.729 --> 00:01:31.010
finally give birth to a pure Elven child.

00:01:31.010 --> 00:01:35.590
However, when Francesca's baby is cruelly
assassinated, the Deathless Mother revels

00:01:35.590 --> 00:01:40.030
in her suffering, which gives her the energy
to break free from her prison in the hut.

00:01:40.030 --> 00:01:44.911
The newly-liberated demon seeks out Ciri,
possesses her, and begins to murder the witchers

00:01:44.911 --> 00:01:47.420
at Kaer Morhen one-by-one.

00:01:47.420 --> 00:01:50.659
Notice how she uses the same dagger that she
used to kill an early witcher.

00:01:50.659 --> 00:01:53.010
Klef here was one of the first witchers.

00:01:53.010 --> 00:01:54.330
That's what she used to kill him.

00:01:54.330 --> 00:01:59.280
So, Voleth Meir is basically using the same
dagger to enact revenge on the school of witchers

00:01:59.280 --> 00:02:01.770
who locked her away all those years ago.

00:02:01.770 --> 00:02:06.049
Although Geralt arrives to try to break Ciri
out of the Deathless Mother's possession,

00:02:06.049 --> 00:02:10.640
the demon is able to keep control of her by
offering her an alternate world in her mind

00:02:10.640 --> 00:02:13.060
where she can be with loved ones she's lost.

00:02:13.060 --> 00:02:17.959
And fans of Bly Manor will notice some interesting
parallels here with that horror story.

00:02:17.959 --> 00:02:23.269
Voleth Meir then uses Ciri's scream to split
open the Witcher Medallion tree, revealing

00:02:23.269 --> 00:02:28.090
a stone monolith which she splits into shards
that attack the witchers, before creating

00:02:28.090 --> 00:02:32.569
a portal that pulls through a pair of basilisk
monsters from another world which she sets

00:02:32.569 --> 00:02:34.060
upon the witchers.

00:02:34.060 --> 00:02:38.650
In fact this moment was foreshadowed in the
fifth episode when Triss and Ciri journeyed

00:02:38.650 --> 00:02:43.349
into the valley of Ciri's soul, and Ciri began
to call out to Geralt who was with Istredd

00:02:43.349 --> 00:02:47.030
at the site of the shattered monolith outside
Cintra.

00:02:47.030 --> 00:02:48.409
Geralt!

00:02:48.409 --> 00:02:49.799
Geralt!

00:02:49.799 --> 00:02:55.040
As Ciri called out, the Medallion Tree at
Kaer Morhen began to crack and vibrate, a

00:02:55.040 --> 00:03:00.140
clue to the hidden stone inside, and shards
of the monolith outside Cintra flew into the

00:03:00.140 --> 00:03:03.010
air and opened up a gateway that released
another monster.

00:03:03.010 --> 00:03:07.699
Istredd who'd been researching monoliths discovered
that they were all connected and that on the

00:03:07.699 --> 00:03:13.059
same day Ciri destroyed the first stone, another
monolith began to vibrate, something which

00:03:13.059 --> 00:03:17.090
led to a new theory about what happened during
the Conjunction of Spheres, the event that

00:03:17.090 --> 00:03:18.469
collided worlds together.

00:03:18.469 --> 00:03:22.019
If the original spheres are still out there
somewhere and our monoliths are calling to

00:03:22.019 --> 00:03:23.930
them…
then the monsters aren't new.

00:03:23.930 --> 00:03:25.999
And they're using our monoliths as gateways.

00:03:25.999 --> 00:03:31.019
Although the witchers manage to slay the basilisks,
the Deathless Mother remains firmly in control

00:03:31.019 --> 00:03:35.459
of Ciri keeping her tucked away in the happy
memories of her long-dead family.

00:03:35.459 --> 00:03:37.829
I'm staying right here.

00:03:37.829 --> 00:03:38.829
Forever.

00:03:38.829 --> 00:03:43.489
Geralt realises the only option is to find
an alternate vessel to Ciri to contain the

00:03:43.489 --> 00:03:48.629
demon, which leads to Yen sacrificing herself
in a call-back to her attempted suicide in

00:03:48.629 --> 00:03:53.159
Season 1, something also foreshadowed in her
vision with the Deathless Mother.

00:03:53.159 --> 00:03:57.669
For Yennefer, this is the moment to right
the wrong she did to Ciri by almost delivering

00:03:57.669 --> 00:04:02.900
her to Voleth Meir, and the spell she casts
pulls the demon out of Ciri and into her.

00:04:02.900 --> 00:04:07.609
Notice how Yen's eyes finally become purple
again at this point because this is the moment

00:04:07.609 --> 00:04:11.859
her magic returns after being depowered for
most of the second season.

00:04:11.859 --> 00:04:13.879
I felt it come back when I…

00:04:13.879 --> 00:04:16.040
When you sacrificed yourself for Ciri.

00:04:16.040 --> 00:04:20.810
Next though, to get the monster out of Yennefer,
Ciri uses her own powers to take herself,

00:04:20.810 --> 00:04:22.830
Geralt and Yen into another world.

00:04:22.830 --> 00:04:28.410
As they all land on another sphere, the demon
leaves Yen and reforms itself as one of a

00:04:28.410 --> 00:04:33.340
group of apocalyptic riders which fans of
The Witcher 3 game and the books will recognise

00:04:33.340 --> 00:04:34.570
as The Wild Hunt.

00:04:34.570 --> 00:04:39.910
The Wild Hunt is a group of antagonists who
are associated with being an omen of doom,

00:04:39.910 --> 00:04:44.350
appearing before or during times of war, and
they were mentioned this way a couple of times

00:04:44.350 --> 00:04:45.700
in Season 2.

00:04:45.700 --> 00:04:48.630
The Wild Hunt walks among us!

00:04:48.630 --> 00:04:53.940
They're known for travelling between realms
and kidnapping people to use as slaves and

00:04:53.940 --> 00:04:58.810
they're clearly after Ciri specifically because
of her exceptional powers.

00:04:58.810 --> 00:05:04.190
Child of the Elder Blood, starry-eyed Daughter
of Chaos, join our Hunt.

00:05:04.190 --> 00:05:06.140
Your place is among us.

00:05:06.140 --> 00:05:11.030
By the way, not only does the reddish colouring
of this world give it hellish, apocalyptic

00:05:11.030 --> 00:05:15.900
feel, but it may also be an allusion to the
name "Red Riders" that the Wild Hunt are sometimes

00:05:15.900 --> 00:05:17.250
known by.

00:05:17.250 --> 00:05:22.220
The Wild Hunt also appeared during the journey
into Ciri's deep subconscious when she discovered

00:05:22.220 --> 00:05:24.430
she's a descendant of Lara Dorren.

00:05:24.430 --> 00:05:28.860
Notice the little blue flowers here around
the dying elf which only grow wherever Elder

00:05:28.860 --> 00:05:33.360
Blood has been spilled, like the ones which
grew from Ciri's blood around Kaer Morhen.

00:05:33.360 --> 00:05:37.230
Lara Dorren was an Elven sorceress who had
a child with a human mage;

00:05:37.230 --> 00:05:42.390
however, their union was controversial among
both humans and elves, which led to Lara's

00:05:42.390 --> 00:05:43.510
persecution.

00:05:43.510 --> 00:05:47.910
When Istredd visits Codringher and Fenn, he
learns about the curse Lara placed before

00:05:47.910 --> 00:05:51.410
she died
'My curse will hound your descendants unto

00:05:51.410 --> 00:05:53.160
the tenth generation.'

00:05:53.160 --> 00:05:59.310
'Until the columns of time and space tremble
and open for my people.'

00:05:59.310 --> 00:06:02.280
'Then my vengeance will be born again.'

00:06:02.280 --> 00:06:07.170
The curse alludes to Ciri's screams and her
effect on the monoliths which have now opened

00:06:07.170 --> 00:06:10.580
portals in space-time that allow inter-dimensional
travel,

00:06:10.580 --> 00:06:15.270
and it also ties in with Ithillinne's Prophecy
that predicts the end of the world, a part

00:06:15.270 --> 00:06:24.460
of which Lara Dorren recites to Ciri during
her mind journey with Triss.

00:06:24.460 --> 00:06:28.170
The world will die amidst frost and be reborn
of the new sun.

00:06:28.170 --> 00:06:29.327
Reborn of Elder blood, of the seed that has
been sown.

00:06:29.327 --> 00:06:30.327
A seed that will not sprout, but will burst
into flame.

00:06:30.327 --> 00:06:34.190
Elder blood is a gene that tends to pass on
more in the female line, and although Calanthe

00:06:34.190 --> 00:06:38.560
possessed it herself, the Queen tried to supress
knowledge of her Elven heritage.

00:06:38.560 --> 00:06:42.480
And Ciri witnesses that fear herself when
she sees her mother and father arguing over

00:06:42.480 --> 00:06:44.940
the discovery of Ciri's Elven descent.

00:06:44.940 --> 00:06:46.300
They'd kill her if they knew.

00:06:46.300 --> 00:06:47.300
It's a prophecy.

00:06:47.300 --> 00:06:48.300
Maybe it's not true.

00:06:48.300 --> 00:06:49.760
[Duny] It doesn't matter if it's true.

00:06:49.760 --> 00:06:52.780
It only matters if the people believe it.

00:06:52.780 --> 00:06:57.800
And Duny was right because Triss is truly
terrified after what she sees in Ciri, and

00:06:57.800 --> 00:07:02.060
reports the matter back to the Brotherhood
at Aretuza who by the end of the season decide

00:07:02.060 --> 00:07:05.830
to place a bounty on Ciri and anyone protecting
her.

00:07:05.830 --> 00:07:10.130
And talking of Duny, the big twist reveal
at the end is that Ciri's father is still

00:07:10.130 --> 00:07:14.400
alive and is actually Emperor Emhyr, aka the
White Flame.

00:07:14.400 --> 00:07:19.130
In fact, there was a little hint in Ciri's
dreamworld that her father was still alive,

00:07:19.130 --> 00:07:24.150
because notice how everyone from Mousesack
to Calanthe and Pavetta fade away to dust,

00:07:24.150 --> 00:07:25.150
but he doesn't.

00:07:25.150 --> 00:07:26.150
In the books, Emhyr was the heir to the Nilfgaardian
throne, until his father was overthrown by

00:07:26.150 --> 00:07:27.150
someone known as the Usurpur, who had a sorcerer
curse Emhyr and turn him into a hedgehog-human

00:07:27.150 --> 00:07:28.150
hybrid.

00:07:28.150 --> 00:07:29.150
Emyhr fled Nilfgaard and ended up going under
the alias Duny, keeping his original identity

00:07:29.150 --> 00:07:30.150
a secret even after he married Pavetta.

00:07:30.150 --> 00:07:31.150
Ciri and her family had assumed Duny died
on the sea voyage he took with his wife;

00:07:31.150 --> 00:07:36.420
however, there's a secret reason why he survived
which will take us into likely Season 3 spoiler

00:07:36.420 --> 00:07:42.190
territory so you can skip forward to this
timestamp in case you don't want to know yet.

00:07:42.190 --> 00:07:46.800
In the books, Duny planned to use the sea
voyage as a way to secretly disappear with

00:07:46.800 --> 00:07:52.370
Pavetta and Ciri to Nilfgaard, by faking their
death at sea with the assistance of the mage

00:07:52.370 --> 00:07:53.370
Vilgefortz.

00:07:53.370 --> 00:07:57.790
However, when Pavetta discovered the plan,
she decided to get Ciri off the boat before

00:07:57.790 --> 00:07:58.980
it set sail.

00:07:58.980 --> 00:08:03.760
This led to an argument later at sea where
Duny accidentally pushed Pavetta overboard

00:08:03.760 --> 00:08:04.760
where she drowned.

00:08:04.760 --> 00:08:10.010
Vilgefortz then ported Duny and himself off
the boat which led everyone to assume Duny

00:08:10.010 --> 00:08:11.980
had also died on the trip.

00:08:11.980 --> 00:08:16.430
In the meantime, Duny returned to reclaim
his position as Emperor of Nilfgaard as well

00:08:16.430 --> 00:08:18.920
as his former name Emhyr.

00:08:18.920 --> 00:08:22.940
Another twist Emhyr reveals is that he was
the one who ordered the murder of Francesca's

00:08:22.940 --> 00:08:27.480
Elven baby, which meant he knew Cahir and
Fringilla were lying to him;

00:08:27.480 --> 00:08:31.090
so they end up carted off by Nilfgaardian
soldiers.

00:08:31.090 --> 00:08:35.839
Having the baby killed sends Francesca and
the elves north to Nilfgaard's enemy, Redania,

00:08:35.839 --> 00:08:41.300
who they believe are to blame for the baby's
death, and Francesca carries out some infanticide

00:08:41.300 --> 00:08:45.300
of her own as she casts a spell killing all
Redania's babies.

00:08:45.300 --> 00:08:50.040
Francesca also later discovers from Istredd
that Ciri is Hen Ikeir, the Elven term for

00:08:50.040 --> 00:08:54.139
Elder Blood, which means the Elves too now
will be looking for the princess in Season

00:08:54.139 --> 00:09:00.029
3 as they will see her as a possible saviour
who can liberate them from human persecution.

00:09:00.029 --> 00:09:04.860
And lurking in the background of this moment
and many others in Season 2 is Dijkstra's

00:09:04.860 --> 00:09:09.029
spy owl, who is finally revealed as Philippa
at the very end.

00:09:09.029 --> 00:09:11.639
I'm saying word is out about the girl.

00:09:11.639 --> 00:09:13.760
Things just got more fun, Philippa.

00:09:13.760 --> 00:09:19.259
Philippa is a sorceress in the Redanian court
with the ability to polymorph into an owl.

00:09:19.259 --> 00:09:24.089
Notice also the owl feathers on her costume
and the talon-shaped ring on her hand.

00:09:24.089 --> 00:09:28.939
Although Vizimir is the king in Redania, it
seems like Dijkstra together with Philippa

00:09:28.939 --> 00:09:34.089
are the ones really pulling the strings in
the kingdom, given Vizimir's overall apathetic

00:09:34.089 --> 00:09:36.360
attitude to important matters.

00:09:36.360 --> 00:09:38.439
Speaking of which, I'm starving, Dijkstra.

00:09:38.439 --> 00:09:39.439
Get to the point.

00:09:39.439 --> 00:09:43.110
But there's still another twist to reveal
when Dijkstra tells Philippa:

00:09:43.110 --> 00:09:44.110
Bring me the bard.

00:09:44.110 --> 00:09:46.490
It's about time he paid back his benefactor.

00:09:46.490 --> 00:09:51.290
Dijkstra doesn't mention Jaskier by name,
but it's heavily implied that the famous bard

00:09:51.290 --> 00:09:55.910
loved and hated by Geralt, appears to be on
the Redanian payroll.

00:09:55.910 --> 00:10:00.759
This is surprising as I didn't detect any
real hints of an alternate agenda during Jaskier's

00:10:00.759 --> 00:10:06.000
scenes in Season 2 and my best guess is that
his fame with his "Toss A Coin To Your Witcher"

00:10:06.000 --> 00:10:10.480
song put him on Dijkstra's radar as someone
who could potentially spy on the witchers.

00:10:10.480 --> 00:10:15.760
That, or there'll be a new bard who's revealed
as a spy in Season 3.

00:10:15.760 --> 00:10:19.220
Another pair of characters with their own
agenda are Rience and Lydia.

00:10:19.220 --> 00:10:24.220
Rience was initially in jail for crimes during
Calanthe's reign, but when Nilfgaard took

00:10:24.220 --> 00:10:29.860
over the city, Lydia came to him with an offer
of freedom in return for hunting down Ciri.

00:10:29.860 --> 00:10:33.890
During this mission, he ended up getting half
his face burned by Yennefer, an interesting

00:10:33.890 --> 00:10:38.240
change from the books which I explain in my
easter eggs and things you missed video.

00:10:38.240 --> 00:10:43.300
Rience managed to steal the vial of Ciri's
blood from Kaer Morhen which he took to Lydia

00:10:43.300 --> 00:10:46.279
who attempted to perform blood tracing on
the sample.

00:10:46.279 --> 00:10:50.660
This went badly for her, as we discover in
the finale, where we see she suffered significant

00:10:50.660 --> 00:10:55.470
injuries from the experiment that burned off
part of her face and now she can only communicate

00:10:55.470 --> 00:10:56.470
telepathically.

00:10:56.470 --> 00:10:58.639
I won't let you down again, my lord…

00:10:58.639 --> 00:11:04.259
As for whom Rience and Lydia are talking to,
I suspect strongly in Season 3 it'll be revealed

00:11:04.259 --> 00:11:05.709
to be Vilgefortz.

00:11:05.709 --> 00:11:10.180
In the books, Lydia is the mage's personal
assistant and secretary, and there are clues

00:11:10.180 --> 00:11:12.610
in the show that Vilgefortz has a hidden agenda.

00:11:12.610 --> 00:11:17.050
At the end of the first season, he decided
to murder a Northern solider even though he'd

00:11:17.050 --> 00:11:21.070
gone with the rest of the Brotherhood to Sodden
to defend the North against the Nilfgaardian

00:11:21.070 --> 00:11:22.070
attack.

00:11:22.070 --> 00:11:26.149
And in Season 2, he begins to act strangely
around Tissaia whenever the subject of Ciri

00:11:26.149 --> 00:11:30.330
comes up and he seems to be obsessed with
trying to uncover what Tissaia might be hiding

00:11:30.330 --> 00:11:31.330
about the princess.

00:11:31.330 --> 00:11:32.779
I wouldn't ask you to if it wasn't necessary!

00:11:32.779 --> 00:11:39.350
I expect in Season 3, now that Emhyr's identity
as Ciri's father has been revealed, Vilgefortz's

00:11:39.350 --> 00:11:44.019
true intentions and what he's getting in return
from the Emperor will also be disclosed.

00:11:44.019 --> 00:11:48.129
I'm looking forward to seeing more of the
Redanian Intelligence network and Philippa's

00:11:48.129 --> 00:11:51.670
owl spy next season;
however, in real life, you might be troubled

